In Bot Framework v4, Adaptive Cards are used to create rich and interactive cards for your users. However, the background color of an Adaptive Card is not directly modifiable.

The Adaptive Card specification does not provide a direct way to change the background color of a card. The focus is on the content within the card, not the background.

However, you can create a custom image with the desired background color and use it as the card's image. Here's an example of how you can do this:

```json
{
    "type": "AdaptiveCard",
    "body": [
        {
            "type": "Image",
            "url": "https://your-custom-image-url.png",
            "altText": "Custom Background"
        },
        {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "text": "Your Text Here"
        }
    ],
    "actions": [],
    "style": {
        "spacing": "Medium"
    }
}
```

In this example, replace `"https://your-custom-image-url.png"` with the URL of your custom image. The image should be the same size as the card to avoid distortion.

Remember, the Bot Framework v4 uses the Adaptive Cards 1.0 specification, and some features may not be supported or may behave differently compared to the latest Adaptive Cards specification.

For more information about Adaptive Cards, you can refer to the official documentation: https://adaptivecards.io/explorer/

