First, let's create a `TooltipContext` to store the state of the currently opened Tooltip and a function to close it.

```jsx
import React, { createContext, useState } from 'react';

export const TooltipContext = createContext();

export const TooltipProvider = ({ children }) => {
  const [tooltip, setTooltip] = useState(null);

  const closeTooltip = () => {
    setTooltip(null);
  };

  const value = { tooltip, closeTooltip };

  return (
    <TooltipContext.Provider value={value}>
      {children}
      {tooltip && <div className="tooltip">{tooltip}</div>}
    </TooltipContext.Provider>
  );
};
```

Now, let's create the Tooltip component that uses the `TooltipContext` to open and close the tooltip.

```jsx
import React, { useContext } from 'react';
import { TooltipContext } from './TooltipContext';

const Tooltip = ({ children, placement = 'bottom', content }) => {
  const { tooltip, closeTooltip } = useContext(TooltipContext);

  const handleMouseEnter = () => {
    if (!tooltip) {
      setTooltip({ content, placement });
    }
  };

  const handleMouseLeave = () => {
    if (tooltip && tooltip.content === content) {
      closeTooltip();
    }
  };

  return (
    <div
      onMouseEnter={handleMouseEnter}
      onMouseLeave={handleMouseLeave}
      className="tooltip-trigger"
      role="tooltip"
    >
      {children}
    </div>
  );
};

export default Tooltip;
```

Finally, let's use the Tooltip component in our NextJS app.

```jsx
import Tooltip from '../components/Tooltip';

export default function Home() {
  return (
    <TooltipProvider>
      <div>
        <h1>Hover over me</h1>
        <Tooltip content="This is a tooltip">Hover over the tooltip</Tooltip>
      </div>
    </TooltipProvider>
  );
}
```

Now, when you hover over the "Hover over me" text, the tooltip will open, and when you hover over the tooltip, it will close. If you hover over another Tooltip, the previously opened Tooltip will close, and the new one will open.

